# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  webapp/.env.example  —  copy to .env if you need it:  cp .env.example .env
#  (.env is gitignored — never commit real secrets.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  IMPORTANT: this SQLite app currently reads NO environment variables and has
#  NO secrets hardcoded. The Gemini API key is provided at runtime, not via .env.
#
#  Set the Gemini key on the server in ONE of these ways:
#    1) Admin panel  → log in as admin, paste the key (saved to data/api_key.txt)
#    2) Headless CLI → echo "AIza...your-key..." > data/api_key.txt
#       (data/ is gitignored and persisted via the ./data volume)
#
#  The variables below are documented for reference / future use. Uncomment and
#  wire them up only if you later add python-dotenv loading to the app.

# Gemini (informational — the app reads the key from data/api_key.txt today)
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza_your_key_here
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# Runtime (already set by docker-compose.yml)
# PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
